  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 106 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nRain continues to spread north and east early this afternoon. The \nfirst wave is concentrated across east central SD while a second \nwave is moving into central SD. Areas in between are filling in but \nare battling a layer of very dry air near the sfc with 15 degree \ndewpoint spreads under sfc high pressure. The 18z sounding at ABR \nshows saturation from 700mb up. As the bubble of high pressure \nerodes, the northern edge of the precipitation will continue to \nbattle drier air to the north as the sfc high digs into ND tonight. \nCould see rain taper off Monday morning before it's reinforced by a \nstacked low moving out of Colorado and into the Plains.\n\nAs models rotate the upper low and 700mb low into central SD Monday \nafternoon and evening, forcing and ascent are expected to increase \nwhich will enhance precipitation. With the sfc low in central NE, \nthere has been a notable shift in precip, though, farther south and \neast Monday. Snow potential now covers most of central SD with less \naccumulation expected in Corson county. 90th percentile still shows \nlocal amounts as high as 3 to 4 inches, but located from Eagle Butte \nto Gettysburg with 25th to 75th percentiles ranging from nothing to \nan inch for most areas. As mentioned in previous discussions, models \nhave a notoriously difficult time pinpointing H7 low tracks, so \nconfidence in location and amounts of snow continues to be low. \n\nWith the cloud cover, adjusted hourly temperatures higher overnight \nthan NBM. Blended toward hi-res which account for non-diurnal spread \na bit better. As the low moves northeast Monday night, could \nsee some intensification of precip along the Coteau in the pivot\npoint. A nose of warmer air will keep the precip all rain, \nthough. The system exits Tuesday morning. \n\nTemperatures remain cool through mid week, but a building upper \nridge will push highs back into the 50s and 60s for the latter half \nof the work week before another cold front moves through late \nFriday. This front will also bring additional chances for \nprecipitation for next weekend.",
